# Generated application bundles are reviewed and hashed as binary artifacts.
packages/standards-explorer/dist/standards-explorer.js binary
packages/standards-explorer/dist/standards-explorer.min.js binary

# GENERATED OUTPUT — COMMITTED ON PURPOSE, BUT NOT HAND-REVIEWED.
#
# `lib/` and `dist/` are emitted by `npm run build` from `schema/`. They are
# tracked because consumers fetch them straight from this repository: Go modules
# resolve `lib/go` from the tag, and the release workflow publishes `dist/`
# archives, so untracking them would break both. That makes them build OUTPUT
# that must nonetheless live in git.
#
# The cost was review: a one-schema change arrived as a several-thousand-file
# diff, and the handful of files that actually moved were invisible inside it.
# `linguist-generated` collapses these paths in GitHub's diff view and excludes
# them from language stats, so a pull request shows the SOURCE change first and
# the regenerated output stays one click away rather than in the way.
#
# This is a review affordance, not permission to skip the build: the release
# gate still compares committed output against what CI regenerates, and the Go
# publish step fails outright when `lib/go` disagrees. Regenerate with the full
# `npm run build` (never a single step of it) and commit the whole result.
lib/** linguist-generated=true
dist/** linguist-generated=true

# The archives are gzip streams; a textual diff of them is noise either way.
dist/**/*.tar.gz binary
